const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 16 Walkthrough: Art Supplies Store";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 16 walkthrough for the Art Supplies Store: the 052 drawer code, the two colour-button locks, the mandala canvas and the heart key that ends the level for +50 coins.";
const faqJsonLd = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the 3-digit code in Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 16?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "052. The panel is the white drawer face with an LCD strip and a silver handle, in the back area of the shop near the shelves. Each of the three windows is a cycling digit: tap it and the number goes up by one, wrapping from 9 to 0. Set the windows left to right to 0, 5 and 2 and the drawer releases, holding a tube of tempera and a torn piece of paper."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the 3-digit code for in the Art Supplies Store?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It opens a drawer, not the exit door. The drawer contains a tube of tempera paint and a torn piece of paper. Nothing else in the room takes a three-digit number, so there is only one code to remember in this level."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I unlock the colour-button panels?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Both are colour-sequence locks. The nine-button panel is on a metal safe face and records each press as a coloured dot in the strip above the grid. The four-button panel sits on the top drawer of the white desk and each button cycles through colours as you tap it. Match the order the room's clues give you; a wrong order resets the strip. Our recording does not show the exact colour order clearly enough to print it twice, so we have not published one."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I paint the canvas?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The canvas is the mandala outline on the easel in the back corner. Four shapes get four colours: the four oval petals in the centre are red, the four large clover shapes around them are blue, the four small round dots at the corners between the clovers are yellow, and the curved connecting lines and the background stay white. Anything that does not match the pattern leaves the canvas unfinished."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Where do I get the key for the exit door?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "From behind the picture frame on the back wall. Hang the finished painting in the frame and the frame slides aside, opening a recess with four keys on hooks. The one that fits the pale blue door is the silver key with the heart-shaped bow: the door's keyhole is outlined with the same heart shape."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I finish the Art Supplies Store?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Select the heart-bow Key in the inventory, press Use, and tap the pale blue door with the lever handle. The door opens, the camera pulls back to the shop floor and the level ends on the results panel: +50 coins."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long does Chapter 2 Level 16 take?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Our full recording finishes the level in 8 minutes 28 seconds of level time, and that run stops to read every readable prop. There is no timer and no fail state, so the only thing that stretches the level is the hunt for the drawer code and the two colour locks."}}]};
