      The frame slides aside and leaves a shallow recess in the wall with <b>four keys</b> hanging from small hooks. They are not interchangeable and the game does not label them beyond "Key" for the one you pick. Look at the bows: a plain round bow, a longer oval bow, a silver key with a <b>heart-shaped bow</b>, and an ornate old-fashioned bow with a decorative loop. Take the heart one. It is the only key whose shape is repeated anywhere in the room, and it is repeated on the door.
